[Chapter $2.1$, <<cite:Che95>>] Let $(L, [,])$ be a Lie superalgebra. A Lie-Rinehart superalgebra is a triple $(A,L,\tilde{\alpha})$ equipped with an $A$-module structure on $L$, and an even map $\tilde{\alpha}: L \to s\mathrm{Der}(A)$ which is simultaneously a homomorphism of Lie superalgebras and a homomorphism of $A$-modules such that

\begin{align}
[x, a \cdot y] =(-1)^{\mid a \mid \mid x \mid}a \cdot [x,y] + \tilde{\alpha}(x)(a) \cdot y, \ \forall x,y,\in L, \ a\in A.
\end{align}
